{
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "myspehr",
  "compatibility_date": "2025-09-24",
  "compatibility_flags": ["nodejs_compat"],
  "main": "src/server.ts"
  // NOTE (2026-09-19): a git-triggered build/deploy (e.g. clicking "Retry
  // build" in the Cloudflare dashboard) resets dashboard-only runtime
  // variables that aren't declared here -- learned this after a retry wiped
  // all 6 vars set under Settings -> Variables and secrets. Deliberately NOT
  // fixing this by inlining values into this committed file (even the
  // publishable/non-secret ones) -- keep re-adding them via the dashboard
  // after any full rebuild instead.
  //
  // UPDATE (2026-10-26): this bit us a second time, specifically for
  // FHIR_BASE_URL and FHIR_BEARER_TOKEN -- the backend lost FHIR connectivity
  // again because both were re-added as plain dashboard "Variable" entries
  // instead of "Secret" entries. To be unambiguous going forward:
  //
  //   FHIR_BASE_URL, FHIR_BEARER_TOKEN, and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY MUST
  //   be set as Cloudflare SECRETS, never as plain Variables. In the
  //   dashboard: Settings -> Variables and secrets -> flip the "Secret"
  //   toggle on when adding/editing each one. Plain "Variable" entries are
  //   wiped by any git-triggered rebuild or a manual "Retry build" click;
  //   Secrets persist across both. If FHIR calls start failing again after a
  //   rebuild, this is the first thing to check.
  //
  //   FHIR_BASE_URL looks like it's "just a hostname" and therefore safe to
  //   hardcode here, but it isn't: its value is
  //   https://fhir.medblocks.com/fhir/<opaque-per-tenant-token>, and that
  //   trailing path segment functions as an access token -- Medblocks FHIR
  //   server URLs encode the per-tenant credential directly in the URL path,
  //   not as a separate header or query param. Treat the whole URL as a
  //   secret, not a convenience value, and do NOT commit it into this file
  //   even in a future "cleanup." Same reasoning applies to FHIR_BEARER_TOKEN
  //   (an explicit bearer token, obviously a secret).
  // Custom domain routes (myspehr.live / www.myspehr.live) are deliberately
  // left out for now: wrangler deploy fails with "Can't infer zone from
  // route" [code: 10082] until the domain is actually registered and added
  // as a zone in this Cloudflare account. Add back once that's done:
  //   "routes": [
  //     { "pattern": "myspehr.live", "custom_domain": true },
  //     { "pattern": "www.myspehr.live", "custom_domain": true }
  //   ]
}
